Count a user only once the object exists.  If the constructor throws (e.g.
DxvkInstance when no Vulkan device can be enumerated), the count stayed at
1 with a null object, so the next acquire() returned null and the caller
crashed: CreateDXGIFactory1() failed cleanly, then D3D11CreateDevice()
dereferenced the null instance (read at 0x28 in dxgi.dll).  With this
change every acquire() retries and fails with an error instead.
